		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4476&amp;p=34832#p34832"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Ah, that's a great point I hadn't considered, and yeah in Europe I would definitely want support for Galileo, and whilst I'm happy getting dirty in some code I don't fancy patching a uBlox in. Think I'll stick with the module you linked to then and just apply plenty of the hot snot instead to stop it going everywhere. I'll also take a small connector out the side to give the antenna a better mount, as where it is installed would mostly be shielded.</div></blockquote>I am currently working on support for these M10 class devices, but currently the firmware won't work at all with them because often the default baud rate is not 9600, and although they are configurable using a the uBlox uCenter application to change the baud rate, but changing the baud rate causes other problems, so the best option is for me to add automatic baud rate selection to the firmware.<br><br>I am currently experimenting with putting a Beitian BE122 module in a md9600, which does not have a separate antenna, but may be small enough to glue the entire module were the antenna normally goes.<br><br>At the moment, none of the GPS module manufacturers seem to be making a small M10 class module with separate antenna <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_sad.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":-(" title="Sad"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Dec 20, 2024 7:58 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
