<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Good day. I have also been using this radio for several days, I do not think that I will install GPS, the radio is installed at home and does not move, it is enough to enter the coordinates manually. Perhaps the poor reception is due to the lack of some other parts on the board, as in the md-uv 380 there is still a filter and amplifier missing, perhaps here in V2 something is missing too!? Could you take a photo of the board in the area of ??the GPS module? Excellent radio with excellent firmware, Taking advantage of the moment I want to once again thank the developers for the opportunity to improve my radio using OpenGD77!</div></blockquote>If the radio is mainly used at home, then there is no need for GPS.<br><br>I only fitted the GPS in both my MD9600 because I was interested to see if it was possible and how it performed<br><br>Both these radios have identical modules, but strangely the GPS reception is never identical<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2685&amp;sid=d2cf15b78aae742b32b607345078dd3b" class="postimage" alt="IMG_20241004_163811501.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2686&amp;sid=d2cf15b78aae742b32b607345078dd3b" class="postimage" alt="IMG_20241004_170703879.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2687&amp;sid=d2cf15b78aae742b32b607345078dd3b" class="postimage" alt="IMG_20241012_171445739.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Oct 12, 2024 6:18 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
